  "body": "## What changed\n\n`camcraft-ui --read-only job.camproj` opens a project read-only. The MCP\ntool `open_project` takes `read_only: true` for the same result. A save\nover the opened file is then refused on every save route, and the file\nstays byte for byte. A save to another file works and ends read-only. The\ntitle bar shows `CamCraft - job.camproj (read-only)`.\n\n- One rule, `project::refuse_read_only_save` in `crates/app/src/project/`,\n  refuses a save to the file that the project is open read-only from. The\n  window's `State::save_project_path` and `script::api::v_save` call it.\n  `v_save` serves MCP `save_project`, script `cam.save` and the live MCP\n  seam of a window.\n- The rule compares canonical paths, so a save from the Save As dialog\n  to the opened file is refused too.\n- In the window, Save on a read-only project opens the Save As dialog, as\n  the editor for shipped machines does. The Save of the unsaved-changes\n  prompt does the same.\n- Changes stay allowed in memory.\n- The read-only state is kept next to the document path:\n  `State::project_read_only` in the window, `Env::doc_read_only` in a\n  headless MCP session or a script run. The live seam gets the window's\n  state through `LiveOptions::read_only`.\n- A model file with `--read-only` is imported as usual. A headless start\n  ignores the option. The live seam still refuses `open_project`.\n- The same option name and behaviour as the open SolidCraft proposal\n  for `--read-only` (tangency-labs/solidcraft#20830).\n- No change to the file format or `PROJECT_VERSION`.\n- Docs: the `--help` text, `docs/user-guide/start-options.md`,\n  `site/content/guide/automate/cli.md` and `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md`.\n- Decisions: `docs/decisions/3609-read-only-open.md`.\n\nThis branch starts at upstream/main `60b19abe8`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNew in `crates/app/tests/read_only_open.rs`:\n\n- `the_rule_refuses_only_the_opened_file_of_a_read_only_project`\n- `a_read_only_project_refuses_a_save_over_its_file_and_keeps_it`\n- `a_save_to_another_file_works_and_ends_read_only`\n- `a_plain_open_ends_read_only_and_a_bad_flag_changes_nothing`\n- `a_script_save_after_a_read_only_open_is_refused`\n- `the_live_seam_refuses_an_approved_save_over_a_read_only_window_project`\n\nNew in `crates/ui/src/launch_file_tests.rs`:\n\n- `a_read_only_project_refuses_a_save_over_its_file_and_save_as_ends_read_only`\n- `read_only_changes_nothing_for_a_model_file`\n\nNew in `crates/ui/src/cli_options_tests.rs`:\n\n- `read_only_is_a_switch_that_keeps_the_file_after_it`\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick` (Windows 11, on `60b19abe8` plus this change):\n214 of 216 steps passed. The two red steps are not from this change:\n\n- `example_catalog`: `catalog_2d_drill_overfeed::{rebuilds,regenerates}`.\n  The refusal text is equal, and only the line end is different. The\n  checkout uses `core.autocrlf=true`, so `refusal.txt` has `\\r\\n`.\n- `first_part_programs`: `first_router_part_posts_the_shipped_program`.\n  It also fails on `60b19abe8` (#3574).\n\nThe steps of this change all passed:\n\n- `read_only_open`: 6 passed.\n- `mcp_live`: 14 passed.\n- `mcp_doc_drift`: 6 passed.\n- `mcp`: 24 passed.\n- `scripting`: 20 passed.\n- The app lib tests: 298 passed.\n- The `camcraft-ui` lib tests: 1476 passed, 8 ignored. These include\n  `launch_file_tests` and `cli_options_tests`.\n- The 16 ui suites, among them `gpu_render`, `shell` and `operations`.\n\nThe other app steps are the suites that the gate maps from\n`app::project`, `app::script` and `app::mcp`.\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\nThe gate and clippy ran on this change before the issue existed. The head\ndiffers from that tree only in the issue number: in code comments and in\nthe name of the decision file.\nHeavy lanes: not run (no heavy step for a `P2` or lower PR, #3556).\nReach from `cargo xtask gate heavy --dry-run`: every `app` heavy target\n(212 steps), because `crates/app/src/mcp/live.rs` changed.\n\n## Not in this change\n\n- A read-only open on the live seam. The live seam refuses\n  `open_project`, so that an agent cannot skip the window's\n  unsaved-changes prompt. The window's read-only state still reaches a\n  live `save_project`.\n- A new script form `cam.load(path, options)`. Scripts use\n  `cam.call(\"open_project\", {path, read_only: true})`.\n- `read_only` in `get_job`.\n- The window does not follow the path of a live `save_project` with a\n  new path. This is the behaviour today. The window keeps its path and\n  stays read-only.\n- A reopen from the recent list, or in a later session, is not\n  read-only. The recent list keeps paths only.\n- The read-only bit of the file on disk.\n- A hand-off of the flag to a running window. CamCraft has no\n  single-instance hand-off.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Save As dialog route in the window. A headless test cannot open a\n  native dialog. The tests pin the refusal behind it.\n- The live seam through a real window and the AI chat's Allow prompt.\n  A test calls `answer_live_with` with the options that the window builds.\n- Linux and macOS.\n- A project on a network share.\n\nChangelog: `camcraft-ui --read-only` and `open_project` with `read_only: true` open a project read-only: Save never writes over the opened file, and Save As writes your own copy.\nEffort: medium\n\nFixes #3609\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
